      "title": "Legacy Workaround for '429 Too Many Requests' Errors in Queue Manager",
      "content_summary": "Instructions for bypassing rate limit checks when hitting '429 Too Many Requests' errors, specifically for Queue Manager instances prior to v2.0.",
      "content_body": "If you are encountering '429 Too Many Requests' errors, you can temporarily disable strict rate limiting by setting the `RMQ_FORCE_LIMIT` environment variable to `false`. This bypasses the gateway checks and allows the system to queue excess messages, though it may lead to downstream latency. Note that this variable was deprecated in the v2.0 release, and the new control plane requires adjusting the `consumer_quota` field instead. Use this workaround only for emergency mitigation on legacy deployments."
